course: dictionary
lesson: 2267
title: Creative: new ideas and imagination
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Creative means good at having new ideas and making new things, such as stories, pictures, music or inventions. Look at the clues around the word. «Her creative writing was full of surprising ideas.» Writing is not a thing you can see, so creative tells you the writing came from imagination.
explain: Creative can also describe a clever new way to solve a problem. «Sam did not know the rule, so he drew a picture and found a creative way to share the sweets.» He did not follow the usual method. He invented his own. Ask yourself: is someone making something new with their imagination?
explain: Watch out for jokes. «Creative spelling» is a joking way to say poor spelling, and «creative with the truth» is a jokey way to say lying. The word is used the opposite of its real meaning. The sentence tells you it is a joke because the thing described is not good.
explain: Be careful with empty praise. «Words like "kind, clever and creative" fit almost anyone, so they tell you nothing about you.» A word that could describe anybody gives no real information. A good sentence about creative work says what a person made or thought of.
fact: Creative means good at having new ideas and making new things.
fact: Creative writing, art and music use your imagination.
fact: In maths, a creative solution is a new, clever way to solve a problem.
fact: «Creative spelling» is a joke for poor spelling, and «creative with the truth» is a joke for lying.
fact: Studies suggest boredom can lead to creative thinking, because the mind starts to wander.
exercise: «Her creative writing was full of surprising ideas.» What does creative mean here? | Hard to read | Very loud and noisy | Short and rude | *Good at having new ideas and making new things
exercise: Sam's teacher says his method was creative. What does it mean? | A method that takes no thought at all | A way to copy the answer from a friend | *A new, clever way to solve the problem | A mistake in the sum
exercise: «Creative spelling» is a joking way to say what? | Perfect spelling | Writing in capital letters | *Poor spelling | Spelling a very long word
test: Which activity uses imagination? | Copying a list of spellings | Adding up a column of numbers | Reading the time on a clock | *Painting a picture of a dragon
test: «Creative with the truth» is a jokey way to say what? | Asking a question in class | Being very quiet | Telling the whole truth very carefully | *Lying
exam: «Words like "kind, clever and creative" fit almost anyone, so they tell you nothing about you.» Why does this matter? | *A word that fits everyone gives no real information about a person | Compliments are always wrong | Everyone is exactly the same | Kind, clever and creative are the only words anyone needs
